MESMERISM AND THE END

01:05:54.907 --> 01:05:56.406
OF THE ENLIGHTENMENT IN FRANCE

01:05:57.326 --> 01:06:00.326
MESMER, OU L'EXTASE MAGNÉTIQUE

01:06:16.175 --> 01:06:19.266
ANIMAL MAGNETISM
AND ITS PSYCHOLOGICAL EFFECTS

01:06:22.855 --> 01:06:24.540
KUNIHIKO MAMIYA

01:06:24.541 --> 01:06:26.226
MUSASHINO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY

01:06:41.415 --> 01:06:43.286
MAY CAUSE A "SPASM"...

01:06:43.375 --> 01:06:45.206
FALLS INTO A COMA...

01:06:45.286 --> 01:06:47.875
MESMERISM

01:07:36.636 --> 01:07:40.056
Sakuma, I've found out who our man is.

01:07:41.226 --> 01:07:43.266
Kunihiko Mamiya.

01:07:43.346 --> 01:07:46.806
A psychology student
up until three years ago.

01:07:47.936 --> 01:07:52.025
His professors said he
hardly showed up for classes.

01:07:53.025 --> 01:07:54.945
Yeah, just like you.

01:07:55.525 --> 01:08:00.116
Then he was a live-in part-timer
at a junkyard in Kawasaki.

01:08:01.445 --> 01:08:03.906
That's probably where he got burned.

01:08:04.786 --> 01:08:06.496
Vanished six months ago.

01:08:07.915 --> 01:08:10.915
No, I don't know what he was doing.

01:08:13.125 --> 01:08:16.795
Have you ever heard of Mesmer?

01:08:23.516 --> 01:08:26.096
Okay. Tell me when I get back.

01:09:39.716 --> 01:09:43.426
What's wrong? What happened?

01:09:48.515 --> 01:09:51.765
Don't scare me like that. Are you ill?

01:09:53.565 --> 01:09:55.225
Why are you home now?

01:09:57.435 --> 01:09:59.145
It's nothing.

01:09:59.815 --> 01:10:02.826
He's ill. I've moved him to the hospital.

01:10:02.906 --> 01:10:05.656
-On whose authority?
-My own.

01:10:06.246 --> 01:10:09.036
-Are you trying to take him away from me?
-That's right.

01:10:09.116 --> 01:10:12.456
It's dangerous to let you
keep talking to that man.

01:10:13.916 --> 01:10:15.496
You bastard.

01:10:16.626 --> 01:10:20.466
-Hey! What about Mesmer?
-I'll ask him.

01:10:30.385 --> 01:10:32.095
No one's supposed to see him.

01:10:33.975 --> 01:10:35.145
Open up.

01:10:46.286 --> 01:10:47.445
Move.

01:11:06.805 --> 01:11:10.095
What's wrong? Your hands are shaking.

01:11:17.645 --> 01:11:18.975
I found out.

01:11:20.895 --> 01:11:25.445
Your name is Kunihiko Mamiya.

01:11:27.275 --> 01:11:28.576
Is that right?

01:11:28.656 --> 01:11:32.956
Mamiya, who is this man called Mesmer?

01:11:33.916 --> 01:11:35.076
Who?

01:11:35.706 --> 01:11:37.086
Mesmer.

01:11:38.836 --> 01:11:42.376
At the university you studied about Mesmer

01:11:42.876 --> 01:11:45.086
and hypnotic suggestion.

01:11:46.176 --> 01:11:47.345
What?

01:11:48.676 --> 01:11:50.765
Whether you remember or not,

01:11:51.595 --> 01:11:57.265
I'm going to have you arraigned
on charges of incitement to murder.

01:11:59.355 --> 01:12:01.145
It's over.

01:12:07.195 --> 01:12:09.866
You saw your wife dead, didn't you?

01:12:17.706 --> 01:12:20.376
Your wife is ill, isn't she?

01:12:23.126 --> 01:12:25.506
Is it hard caring for her at home?

01:12:28.385 --> 01:12:31.635
Where did you hear about that?

01:12:32.845 --> 01:12:35.305
The other detective told me.

01:12:39.355 --> 01:12:42.935
Does it bother you,
talking about your wife?

01:12:50.406 --> 01:12:54.246
Anyway, there'll be lots of time.

01:12:56.076 --> 01:12:58.246
You can't get out of here.

01:12:58.746 --> 01:13:02.496
-It's you who wants out.
-I know what you did.

01:13:02.586 --> 01:13:06.876
Tell me whatever you like.
That's why you came, isn't it?

01:13:10.796 --> 01:13:16.176
You planted hypnotic suggestions
in those people's minds.

01:13:16.265 --> 01:13:19.765
It's hard to be a
detective with a crazy wife.

01:13:19.855 --> 01:13:20.895
Shut up.

01:13:20.975 --> 01:13:25.735
You do it by keeping your work and
your family life completely separate.

01:13:25.815 --> 01:13:27.525
How did you do it?

01:13:27.605 --> 01:13:32.576
The detective or the
husband, which is the real you?

01:13:32.656 --> 01:13:34.826
How did you hypnotize them?

01:13:34.906 --> 01:13:37.156
Neither one is the real you.

01:13:38.116 --> 01:13:40.326
There is no real you.

01:13:41.666 --> 01:13:43.206
Your wife knows that, too.

01:13:43.296 --> 01:13:45.206
How did you hypnotize them?

01:13:47.086 --> 01:13:48.256
Watch.

01:13:52.796 --> 01:13:54.095
You're right.

01:13:55.095 --> 01:13:59.635
My wife is a burden. I know.
You don't have to tell me!

01:14:01.935 --> 01:14:03.355
I'm a detective.

01:14:04.105 --> 01:14:08.565
I've been taught never to show
emotion, even with my family.

01:14:08.645 --> 01:14:11.656
And this is the result.

01:14:17.036 --> 01:14:19.246
I don't understand her.

01:14:19.826 --> 01:14:22.876
She doesn't understand what I go through.

01:14:23.456 --> 01:14:27.126
I know it's my fault that it's that way.
So what?

01:14:27.206 --> 01:14:28.666
What else could you do?

01:14:28.756 --> 01:14:31.836
That's right! What other way is there?

01:14:35.555 --> 01:14:36.635
Look,

01:14:37.676 --> 01:14:42.055
you think this is how I wanted to end up?

01:14:42.555 --> 01:14:47.275
We should all relax, enjoy
ourselves, lead peaceful lives.

01:14:47.355 --> 01:14:49.185
But society isn't like that!

01:14:50.485 --> 01:14:54.445
Oh, so society's to blame.

01:14:55.445 --> 01:14:57.406
It's people like you.

01:14:58.496 --> 01:15:05.036
It's guys like you who have
my head about to split open!

01:15:07.376 --> 01:15:12.546
Lunatics like you have it easy
while citizens like me go through hell!

01:15:13.796 --> 01:15:17.845
I spend my whole life taking
care of that wife of mine!

01:15:34.695 --> 01:15:36.275
If it weren't for you...

01:15:39.406 --> 01:15:42.406
things would be fine with my wife and me.

01:15:47.086 --> 01:15:49.086
Her I can forgive...

01:15:51.506 --> 01:15:53.796
but you I can't.

01:16:04.225 --> 01:16:05.725
You're amazing.

01:16:15.945 --> 01:16:18.065
You like that? Hearing me talk?

01:16:19.025 --> 01:16:20.156
Yeah.

01:16:23.786 --> 01:16:25.206
Good.

01:16:26.666 --> 01:16:28.786
Now it's your turn.
I want the whole story.

01:16:30.796 --> 01:16:32.626
All of it.

01:16:37.385 --> 01:16:38.506
What's wrong?

01:16:42.805 --> 01:16:44.935
Can't talk without your lighter?

01:16:50.895 --> 01:16:51.975
Here.

01:17:01.156 --> 01:17:02.945
You're amazing.

01:17:57.756 --> 01:18:02.926
The water will make you calm.

01:18:07.555 --> 01:18:11.805
It will make you happy, empty.

01:18:14.565 --> 01:18:19.065
You'll be born again, just like me.

01:18:39.336 --> 01:18:40.926
Are you all right?

01:18:42.006 --> 01:18:43.086
Was it you?

01:18:44.796 --> 01:18:47.055
Did you tell him about me?

01:18:47.716 --> 01:18:52.225
Uh, well, you know, he keeps
asking all these questions...

01:19:04.656 --> 01:19:08.286
Mesmer was an 18th-century
Austrian doctor,

01:19:09.246 --> 01:19:11.536
the first man to study hypnosis.

01:19:13.166 --> 01:19:16.626
It wasn't recognized then
as a medical treatment.

01:19:17.416 --> 01:19:21.716
They saw it as fakery, magic,

01:19:22.216 --> 01:19:23.756
or witchcraft.

01:19:25.756 --> 01:19:27.055
And?

01:19:27.135 --> 01:19:30.305
There's still a lot we
don't know about Mesmer.

01:19:31.135 --> 01:19:34.395
Some say he really did
study magic and alchemy.

01:19:37.185 --> 01:19:39.565
And Mamiya's doing that?

01:19:40.185 --> 01:19:41.775
Impossible.

01:19:42.735 --> 01:19:47.366
If so, the diagnosis would be simple.

01:19:48.116 --> 01:19:52.116
He'd simply be a megalomaniac.

01:19:53.826 --> 01:19:55.036
But that's not it.

01:19:55.956 --> 01:20:00.376
He has definitely lost his memory,
but otherwise he's not abnormal.

01:20:01.506 --> 01:20:06.546
But he's also a man with
a very complex personality.

01:20:08.506 --> 01:20:11.466
I see. Okay.

01:20:18.475 --> 01:20:19.725
Takabe.

01:20:21.605 --> 01:20:23.275
Don't talk to him.

01:20:24.355 --> 01:20:26.315
You don't know what could happen.

01:20:27.985 --> 01:20:29.195
Don't get in too deep.

01:20:31.116 --> 01:20:32.286
I know.

01:21:07.445 --> 01:21:08.445
Takabe.

01:21:15.746 --> 01:21:21.456
Mr. Mamiya, could you tell
us your name or date of birth?

01:21:22.456 --> 01:21:24.456
Anything you remember.

01:21:30.966 --> 01:21:32.135
Well?

01:21:32.676 --> 01:21:36.385
Do you remember anything about yourself?

01:21:40.095 --> 01:21:41.145
No.

01:21:41.935 --> 01:21:43.145
Mr. Mamiya,

01:21:44.145 --> 01:21:48.315
are you aware of the
situation you are in at present?

01:21:50.616 --> 01:21:53.195
I mean the charges against you.

01:21:55.536 --> 01:21:56.826
Who are you?

01:21:57.866 --> 01:21:59.786
Fujiwara, from headquarters.

01:22:01.286 --> 01:22:02.706
Well, Mr. Mamiya?

01:22:03.916 --> 01:22:08.216
Do you understand why you're here now?

01:22:08.716 --> 01:22:10.126
What?

01:22:10.216 --> 01:22:12.756
Don't ask questions, answer them.

01:22:12.845 --> 01:22:14.135
What questions?

01:22:14.635 --> 01:22:15.765
Mr. Mamiya,

01:22:16.975 --> 01:22:20.845
incitement to murder can
carry the death penalty.

01:22:21.555 --> 01:22:24.065
Do you understand that?

01:22:24.145 --> 01:22:25.975
Is that your boss?

01:22:26.475 --> 01:22:27.645
Yes.

01:22:29.985 --> 01:22:31.485
That must be a drag.

01:22:31.565 --> 01:22:34.616
Mr. Mamiya, answer my question.

01:22:35.616 --> 01:22:36.945
Who are you?

01:22:38.246 --> 01:22:41.076
-Fujiwara. Headquarters.
-Who?

01:22:41.166 --> 01:22:43.416
-Are you being smart?
-Who are you?

01:22:46.796 --> 01:22:49.836
Takabe, what's wrong with this man?

01:22:50.336 --> 01:22:52.966
-I'm asking who you are.
-Answer my question!

01:22:53.926 --> 01:22:57.466
All right, I'll ask you again.

01:22:59.345 --> 01:23:01.305
Fujiwara-of-Headquarters.

01:23:02.805 --> 01:23:04.105
Who are you?

01:23:06.815 --> 01:23:10.525
What... exactly do you mean?

01:23:12.565 --> 01:23:14.565
You think about that.

01:23:20.996 --> 01:23:22.246
I'm very sorry!

01:23:23.206 --> 01:23:26.416
You must understand, he has amnesia.

01:23:29.546 --> 01:23:31.376
What a bunch.

01:23:35.546 --> 01:23:37.756
They don't understand, do they?

01:23:39.885 --> 01:23:41.265
About me,

01:23:42.265 --> 01:23:43.645
or about you.

01:23:48.355 --> 01:23:52.855
Detective, do you hear my voice?

01:23:55.985 --> 01:23:57.366
You do, don't you?

01:24:00.076 --> 01:24:04.456
That proves you're a special person.

01:24:08.246 --> 01:24:10.126
You knew that from the start.

01:24:12.666 --> 01:24:14.336
So did I.

01:24:16.546 --> 01:24:18.635
You're different from them.

01:24:22.926 --> 01:24:24.265
You're someone

01:24:25.515 --> 01:24:30.105
who can understand what I'm really saying.

01:24:37.025 --> 01:24:38.025
Take him away.

01:26:55.336 --> 01:26:57.256
Will Okinawa be warm?

01:27:00.876 --> 01:27:02.635
Let's eat lots of good food.

01:27:05.426 --> 01:27:07.765
What do you want to eat?

01:27:10.595 --> 01:27:14.145
Fumie, we're not going to Okinawa.

01:27:15.725 --> 01:27:16.815
I know.

01:27:25.775 --> 01:27:30.406
The sea there must be beautiful.

01:27:36.376 --> 01:27:39.046
Just until my work settles down.

01:27:40.336 --> 01:27:41.756
I understand.

01:27:42.336 --> 01:27:43.626
I'll take her bag.

01:27:44.716 --> 01:27:46.216
Shall we go?

01:27:51.475 --> 01:27:53.975
Thank you, Doctor.

01:27:56.765 --> 01:27:58.225
Mr. Takabe.

01:28:00.315 --> 01:28:02.815
It's not good to work too hard.

01:28:05.315 --> 01:28:09.695
You look sicker than your wife to me.

01:28:16.286 --> 01:28:20.586
I'm sorry, I don't have the tag.
I wonder where it went.

01:28:21.086 --> 01:28:24.426
-A week ago, wasn't it?
-Yes.

01:28:25.966 --> 01:28:27.506
Mr. Takabe?

01:28:27.595 --> 01:28:29.756
One moment, please.

01:28:48.235 --> 01:28:50.445
I'm sorry, sir, but it's not here.

01:28:51.485 --> 01:28:53.326
That can't be.

01:28:55.156 --> 01:28:57.786
Maybe you took it somewhere else?

01:28:57.876 --> 01:28:58.996
No.

01:28:59.086 --> 01:29:01.206
Or you gave it to your wife.

01:29:01.296 --> 01:29:02.546
No.

01:29:12.555 --> 01:29:14.135
May I take your plate?

01:29:15.975 --> 01:29:17.185
Yes.

01:29:27.195 --> 01:29:28.355
Yeah?

01:29:29.695 --> 01:29:30.906
Sakuma?

01:29:32.576 --> 01:29:33.735
What?

01:29:35.656 --> 01:29:37.246
No, I'm not busy.

01:29:39.206 --> 01:29:40.206
Now?

01:29:46.836 --> 01:29:48.966
I want to show you something.

01:29:49.635 --> 01:29:50.796
What?

01:29:50.885 --> 01:29:55.176
A film on hypnotherapy.
The university put it on video.

01:29:58.225 --> 01:30:03.815
The oldest material on hypnotism in Japan.

01:30:05.775 --> 01:30:10.105
It probably dates from
the end of the 19th century.

01:30:21.416 --> 01:30:23.706
Watch the man's hand.

01:30:27.256 --> 01:30:31.176
You have to look closely. See? There.

01:30:31.966 --> 01:30:34.805
You see what looks like an X?

01:30:49.065 --> 01:30:51.315
-That's it?
-Yeah.

01:30:52.406 --> 01:30:53.656
What does it mean?

01:30:54.576 --> 01:30:59.406
Her name was Suzu Murakawa.
She was treated for hysteria.

01:30:59.996 --> 01:31:01.956
That's all that's recorded.

01:31:04.286 --> 01:31:06.666
Police records say...

01:31:08.796 --> 01:31:15.046
she was arrested for the
murder of her son in 1898.

01:31:17.926 --> 01:31:21.725
She seems to have killed him

01:31:22.265 --> 01:31:26.895
by carving the shape
of a cross into his neck.

01:31:29.185 --> 01:31:31.105
That's all we know.

01:31:32.695 --> 01:31:35.116
Did Mamiya see this film?

01:31:35.866 --> 01:31:37.195
I don't know.

01:31:37.945 --> 01:31:41.746
There's not much chance even
medical students would see it.

01:31:43.036 --> 01:31:46.876
But even if he had,

01:31:48.206 --> 01:31:52.876
that still wouldn't explain his actions.

01:31:57.676 --> 01:32:00.176
Who's this man in the film?

01:32:01.515 --> 01:32:02.685
Unknown.

01:32:03.725 --> 01:32:09.185
We do know, however, why he
didn't show his face to the camera.

01:32:11.935 --> 01:32:17.025
You know what they called
hypnotism in Japan back then?

01:32:19.985 --> 01:32:21.326
"Soul conjuring."

01:32:22.406 --> 01:32:26.376
Like clairvoyance,
spiritualism — that sort of thing.

01:32:28.456 --> 01:32:34.086
The authorities in any age
always suppress occultism...

01:32:36.426 --> 01:32:41.265
and the Meiji government back then
would have suppressed this technique.

01:32:42.426 --> 01:32:48.265
It would only have been
performed in secret ceremonies.

01:33:34.275 --> 01:33:37.315
HERESIES

01:33:43.036 --> 01:33:47.156
CHAPTER 4 — MESMER

01:33:49.626 --> 01:33:53.166
TOJIRO HAKURAKU DOB UNKNOWN,
DIED IN 1898

01:35:39.275 --> 01:35:40.435
Sakuma.

01:35:50.656 --> 01:35:51.656
Huh?

01:35:52.616 --> 01:35:55.876
So what is Mamiya, then?

01:35:57.836 --> 01:36:00.706
What's your guess? Tell me.

01:36:02.836 --> 01:36:04.176
A missionary.

01:36:05.466 --> 01:36:06.796
A missionary?

01:36:08.256 --> 01:36:11.635
Sent to propagate the ceremony.

01:36:16.935 --> 01:36:20.225
Sorry, I was just imagining things.

01:36:22.485 --> 01:36:24.695
What am I saying?

01:36:25.315 --> 01:36:28.326
Don't take me seriously.

01:36:29.906 --> 01:36:31.536
I'm a little tired.

01:36:33.156 --> 01:36:35.206
Let's call it a day.

01:36:35.956 --> 01:36:38.996
Now I'm getting in too deep.

01:36:48.796 --> 01:36:52.015
Sakuma, what's that?

01:37:00.565 --> 01:37:03.105
Oh, that?

01:37:03.985 --> 01:37:07.406
I just thought it might help me to think.

01:37:07.906 --> 01:37:09.235
About what?

01:37:10.445 --> 01:37:13.116
About...

01:37:15.826 --> 01:37:17.116
I don't know.

01:37:23.756 --> 01:37:25.796
You met Mamiya, didn't you?

01:37:25.876 --> 01:37:27.126
No.

01:37:29.006 --> 01:37:30.095
Yes, you did.

01:37:32.055 --> 01:37:33.385
It's weird.

01:37:35.635 --> 01:37:37.095
I don't remember.

01:39:39.176 --> 01:39:42.225
Kunihiko Mamiya's whereabouts unknown.

01:39:42.305 --> 01:39:48.685
Earlier reports of him near
Kawasaki Station were inaccurate.

01:39:49.185 --> 01:39:52.195
In the absence of further information,

01:39:52.275 --> 01:39:56.826
the search area is being
widened from Tokyo and Saitama

01:39:56.906 --> 01:39:59.695
to the entire Kanto plain.

01:40:01.036 --> 01:40:02.156
Hello?

01:40:03.116 --> 01:40:05.036
One moment, please.

01:40:05.916 --> 01:40:07.916
Mr. Takabe, it's for you.

01:40:09.416 --> 01:40:10.586
Hello?

01:40:12.586 --> 01:40:14.086
I see.

01:40:15.756 --> 01:40:17.885
We're on our way.

01:40:43.956 --> 01:40:47.246
Dr. Sakuma's body has
been taken to the hospital.

01:40:48.666 --> 01:40:53.046
It was probably suicide.
He strangled himself.

01:40:55.216 --> 01:40:57.385
He'd cuffed himself to that pipe,

01:40:58.296 --> 01:40:59.805
strange as that sounds.

01:44:01.525 --> 01:44:03.815
So you've come, Detective.

01:44:16.786 --> 01:44:18.666
Why did you let me escape?

01:44:23.796 --> 01:44:25.216
You know why?

01:44:26.966 --> 01:44:32.595
By letting me escape, you
could learn my true secret.

01:44:34.225 --> 01:44:35.805
All by yourself.

01:44:40.645 --> 01:44:42.895
You didn't have to, though.

01:44:45.315 --> 01:44:51.286
Anyone who wants to meet his
true self is bound to come here.

01:44:52.326 --> 01:44:54.036
It's fate.

01:45:14.515 --> 01:45:15.765
Remember now?

01:45:17.765 --> 01:45:20.605
Do you remember everything?

01:45:28.735 --> 01:45:29.906
You do?

01:45:32.326 --> 01:45:35.786
This is the end for you, too.

01:46:48.445 --> 01:46:51.195
Fearsome... heart of...

01:46:51.866 --> 01:46:53.945
His... healing hand.

01:46:54.025 --> 01:46:57.286
Road of healing... Not a long...

01:46:57.366 --> 01:46:59.996
Take sword...

01:47:00.496 --> 01:47:03.836
A man... but dew.

01:47:03.916 --> 01:47:09.216
Heal, O... water grass! O winter...

01:47:09.296 --> 01:47:10.796
falls... snow.

01:47:10.876 --> 01:47:12.385
That... heal... snow.

01:47:12.466 --> 01:47:14.845
Take... in hand... heal.

01:47:47.496 --> 01:47:49.006
Shall I bring your coffee?

01:47:54.385 --> 01:47:55.506
Yes?

01:47:58.385 --> 01:48:02.055
All right. Bring the car around.

01:48:21.956 --> 01:48:23.286
Here you are.

01:48:24.036 --> 01:48:25.786
-Thanks.
-You're welcome.

01:49:33.435 --> 01:49:36.195
KOJI YAKUSHO

01:49:36.275 --> 01:49:38.985
TSUYOSHI UJIKI

01:49:39.065 --> 01:49:41.616
ANNA NAKAGAWA

01:49:42.406 --> 01:49:43.866
YUKIJIRO HOTARU

01:49:43.945 --> 01:49:45.156
YORIKO DOGUCHI

01:49:45.246 --> 01:49:46.536
DENDEN

01:49:46.616 --> 01:49:47.916
REN OSUGI

01:49:47.996 --> 01:49:49.576
MASAHIRO TODA

